{
  "_about": "How crash report text is redacted. `tokens`: the credential rule the server applies to every stored string and the Android app to the report before it is saved; both test against these. A credential is the word after \"Bearer\" (any case, after spaces only) or a run of at least 32 letters, digits, `-` and `_` with both letters and digits; it becomes `[removed]`. `device`: Android only, because they need what the device knows: `hosts`, the server hosts it redacts (the default server and the ones the player set), and `token`, the stored device token. Each whole host, with an IP address Java prints after it (`host/203.0.113.7`), becomes `[server]`; a longer host name containing it is kept. The stored token becomes `[removed]` wherever it appears. The token rule applies after both. A case with `\"in\": \"preference_key\"` is the name of a preference in `SHARED_PREFERENCES`, not a value: both redact key names as they redact strings, because a key can hold a server or a credential (AnkiQuest keeps records per server under keys like `ankiquestUploadedThrough:https://quest.example.net/hill`). Without `in`, the case is a string.",
  "version": 1,
